Only true for sports car.  Luxury SUV buyers shift focus to new domestic cars now.  The second hand top-end luxury car price dropped about 30% in a year, I mean the models like GLE AMG/RS6 and so on. Even the sports car price is dropping now,  I saw dealers selling brand new M2 and Supra 20% below original tag price.  The login behind the seen is cheap and powerful motors. It give Chinese brand a chance to catch up Germans's engine. With equally powerful platform, Chinese are always good at making  more functional product at lower cost. Just the same story again, remember how TV/Smart Phone or other market been taken by us? 
BTW,  you can have a look of Lixiang L9 or Huawei M9, the interior is so much batter compare to GLS or X6.
@jackt1400

@Darkmatter321you never lived in China. If you ever had you would know the problems with China being in charge. It’s top down and does not give a hoot about anything other than the party. 

Right now China is subsidising its top-end industries like EVs and chips and it’s just undercutting everyone else through uncompetitive practices. Look at that car in this video and tell me what it really does thats any different than a model 3 or Y from Tesla? Certainly nothing in the video differentiates them. 

That said EV cars are more than a fad and other car makers need to adapt. The electric grid and infrastructure is being built up fast here in the US. And with an EV you can charge overnight and never have to fill up a tank outside of road-trips. If EU and Japanese car makers don’t get serious about EVs watch out.

@dna9838 You're talking about a government that's been led by only one party for most of its history. It's hardly possible for the people to exercise their right to replace a democratic regime, unless you want to move the goalposts of what a democratic regime is.

As for suppression of the population, Japan's culture of hierarchical bureaucracy and tradition of public shame is what prevents technological advancements from enhancing daily conveniences, including methods of intelligence such as public surveillance and safety. Technology isn't the only means of freedom and control for the greater masses, something the contemporary West often fails to grasp, and the rest of the world understands all too well.

That Japan has been highly resistant to cultural shifts despite mounting domestic pressure indicates that there's still people at the top holding the reins. Modern Japan hasn't eliminated the members of the aristocracy - their powers have simply transitioned over to capital.

@RoonMian  Look up what the US gov are doing with car manufacturers.
